rekrutacja, chaotic female elven Priestess, ascended.

This is my third ascension. After ascending Wizard and Valkyrie i
thought, that it will be relativy easy to ascend again. It was not. My
Priests kept dying and dying. It's really hard to keep their
experience low early in the game, and they are really pathetic
fighters later.

This one was simply lucky: with early wand of poly his companion
orange dragon helped him clean the way thru dungeon. The rest was
quite straightforward. I was playing very carefully, without taking
any risk. No challenges. Just doing what had to be done. I had no
magic resistance and poison resistance until castle, so i had to be
careful...

I found my own bones in Gehennom which gave me a second, little bit
better ascension kit. Previously i died due to lich and mind flayer,
so this time i genocided them as soon as i could do it.

I learned how to use cancellation to create water. This is very
important trick!

I prepared for final run properly for the first time. Genocided all
the troublesome monsters (and some more by mistake :)Read all the
books, had lots of holy water and options of healing, backup weapon
and important rings (and i needed them!).

Run was uneventfull. Only once had the mysterious force which just
stopped me on the same level few turns from stairs up. Rodney once
Double Troubled, but wands of death have been all i needed to stop
him.

On planes i used conflict, until i encountered two Archons on water
and decided to charm them. They followed me to the end.

BTW: below i listed only spells i used most: this made quite an
effective, but unusual for me, strategy. Usually i rely on attacking
spells and sleep to get rid of monsters. This time i runned away most
of the time.

The first altar was Famine and neutral. Got no problem here.

But second was Pestilence, and this was the only serious issue during
this game - once i was down to 30 HP in few turns and run out of wand
of death charges.

However the second altar was chaotic and didn't have to use helm of
opposite alingemnt. I would use it in case it was lawful, but it was
not...

